Description: Enable Wayland session restore on GNOME again.
 Mozilla bug 2070815 disabled it on GNOME because of the name_in_use protocol error from Mutter, which
 wayland-session-restore-new-ids.patch fixes. Session restore stays disabled where GTK 3 lacks the
 xdg-toplevel-realized signal, by the check right after the removed one.
Author: Mitar
Bug: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2064100
Forwarded: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340272
Applied-Upstream: 162, https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/commit/fcd09a257c7a2778aded5758c8fe645c30964835
Last-Update: 2026-11-23
diff --git a/widget/gtk/nsAppShell.cpp b/widget/gtk/nsAppShell.cpp
--- a/widget/gtk/nsAppShell.cpp
+++ b/widget/gtk/nsAppShell.cpp
@@ -627,12 +627,6 @@ bool nsAppShell::IsSessionRestoreSupported() {
       LOGW("nsAppShell::IsSessionRestoreSupported(): disabled by pref.");
       return false;
     }
-    if (IsGnomeDesktopEnvironment()) {
-      LOGW(
-          "nsAppShell::IsSessionRestoreSupported(): disabled due to Bug "
-          "2064100.");
-      return false;
-    }
 
     GType waylandWindowType = g_type_from_name("GdkWaylandWindow");
